# Copy to .devcontainer/devcontainer.env (GITIGNORED — see the repo's .gitignore) and fill in.
#
# Passed to `docker run` via the "runArgs": ["--env-file", ...] in devcontainer.json, so it
# is picked up automatically at container start. Nothing needs to be exported in the shell
# that launched VS Code, and none of it is baked into an image layer.

# Your GitHub personal access token. This IS a secret — treat it like a password.
#
# Create it under Settings -> Developer settings -> Personal access tokens. Scopes:
#   repo       to read/write issues, PRs, and push over HTTPS
#   read:org   for org-owned repos
#   gist       for the full gh feature set
#
# GH_TOKEN is the variable gh reads natively, so it is used as-is with nothing written to
# disk. Rotating the token is just: edit this file, then reconnect. No rebuild needed.
#
# For GitHub Enterprise, set the feature's "host" option to your instance — gh reads
# GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN for non-github.com hosts, and the feature exports it for you.
GH_TOKEN=
